  "worked_solution": "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A:$ It is not raining.\n\n- The consequent is $B:$ You can go to the beach.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A⇒B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB⇒A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\,$ If you can go to the beach, then it is not raining.",
